{"content":"The fix is complete. Root cause: in sqlparse/filters/aligned_indent.py's `_process_case`, the condition_width list comprehension had an inverted ternary: `0 if cond else len(' '.join(map(str, cond)))`. This meant real conditions (truthy `cond`) got width 0, while `None` conditions (ELSE/END entries) tried to `map(str, None)`, raising `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable`.

Fixed by swapping the branches to `len(' '.join(map(str, cond))) if cond else 0`, so conditions get correct widths and None entries get 0.

Verified manually that both the plain CASE statement and the CASE ... BETWEEN ... AND ... statement now format correctly under `reindent_aligned=True` without error, with proper alignment of WHEN/ELSE/END clauses. No test directory exists in this workspace to run the hidden suite locally, but the fix directly targets the reported TypeError and only touches the CASE-specific width computation, leaving all other alignment behavior unchanged.","tool_calls":[{"id":"final_1","name":"finish","arguments":{"summary":"Fixed regression in sqlparse/filters/aligned_indent.py's AlignedIndentFilter._process_case: the condition_width computation had an inverted ternary (`0 if cond else len(' '.join(map(str, cond)))`), causing `map(str, cond)` to be called on None for ELSE/END entries, raising `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable`. Swapped to `len(' '.join(map(str, cond))) if cond else 0` so real WHEN conditions get their correct string width and None entries (ELSE/END) get width 0. Verified with manual tests that `sqlparse.format(sql, reindent_aligned=True)` now correctly formats CASE statements, including ones containing BETWEEN...AND, restoring proper alignment of WHEN/ELSE/END without raising."}}]}
